# Fixture for function_settle_order_test: a chain of functions declared top
# down, each reading the next.  BNG2 2.9.3's writeXML moves only a function's
# direct references ahead of it, so it writes the chain as b, a, c -- out of
# dependency order.  Settled in declaration order, b() read c() before c()
# had been settled, so b(), a() and the rule's rate were 0 at the start.
# With nothing firing nothing re-settled the table, and B never appeared.
# a() = b() = 2*c() = 2*k = 20, so B(t) is Poisson with mean 20 t.
begin model
begin parameters
  k 10
end parameters
begin molecule types
  B()
end molecule types
begin seed species
  B() 0
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules Btot B()
end observables
begin functions
  a() = b()
  b() = 2*c()
  c() = k
end functions
begin reaction rules
  0 -> B()  a()
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
  writeXML()
end actions
